<title>POLAND: Bank Gdanski to lead loan for gas project.</title>
<headline>Bank Gdanski to lead loan for gas project.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Gdanski SA will lead a consortium of three banks to lend 56 million zlotys to a company building the Polish section of a natural gas pipeline from Siberia to Western Europe, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the consortium, which signed a loan agreement on Wednesday with  System Gazociagow Tranzytowych Europol Gaz SA, also included state-owned Pomorski Bank Kredytowy SA and Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych SA (BIG).</p>
<p>Gdanski said Europol would use the loan to finance the land purchases needed for the Polish section of the pipeline.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
